# Testing & Demo Conventions

## Visible Playwright Demo Harness
- Run story demos with:
  ```powershell
  node scripts/demo/run_story_demo.mjs <STORY-ID>
  ```
- Spec lives at `docs/stories/<STORY-ID>.demo.json`. Actions: `goto`, `wait_for`, `click`, `fill`, `select`, `api_call`, `db_check`.
- Generates headed video at `docs/demos/<STORY-ID>/demo.webm` and markdown report at `docs/demos/<STORY-ID>/DEMO.md`.

## UI `data-testid` Standards
- Pages and key interactive elements MUST have deterministic `data-testid` attributes:
  - Page Heading: `data-testid="<module>-<desk>-heading"`
  - Table Rows: `data-testid="<module>-<desk>-row-<id>"`
  - Form Actions: `data-testid="<module>-<action>-btn"`
  - Alert / Banners: `data-testid="<module>-<desk>-success"` or `...-error"`

## Database Test Rules
- **Tagged Test Records:** Use unique prefix tags (e.g. `DEMO-<STORY-ID>-<timestamp>`) for easy auditing and identification.
- **Append-Only Table Rules:** Never execute `DELETE` on append-only audit and version tables (`stu.lifecycle_history`, `doc.document_versions`, `audit.events`).
- **Dev Database Only:** Never run tests or demos against production or staging refs. Use dev ref `azulbaxszsqxymqmlwfe`.
